@startbpmn BP12_ManageBoardColumns
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP12_ManageBoardColumns.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP12_ManageBoardColumns.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - a column carries a role and a name, and they are different things: BR-58
'   - one editor per entity serves adding a lane and renaming one alike, and where a new lane
'     lands is not drawn - BP12.04 orders them. Call site BP12.03 (Insert a column) is RETIRED,
'     its id never reused: UX-04, DRW-11, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-16
'   - four roles, no neutral escape hatch; the advisor and check-out read the role: BR-58
'   - one Backlog column and at least one Done column per template: BR-59
'   - the Backlog role cannot change; a Done role only while another Done remains: BR-60
'   - the consequences of a legal role change are the user's: BR-60
'   - columns come from a template, one per project plus Chores's own: BR-108
'   - the template governs every board of its project with no deviation inside it, so a
'     write here lands on every one of them at once: BR-108, BR-97
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - archiving a whole column's worth of tasks is one of the three archiving acts: BR-23
'   - declining a column deletion's cascade rejects it rather than detaching: BR-18, BR-21
'   - an empty column deletes cleanly: BR-18
'   - the archive is no shield from a deletion: BR-117
'   - where a chain can refuse, the reply names the OUTCOME rather than claiming a write that
'     may not have happened: the editor, the role change and the deletion all answer an outcome,
'     the shape BP05.02 already has: DRW-07, BR-128
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user NAMES a lane, new or not:
'     SA 2026-10-16
'   - the role box carries the act, not the picking: the user SETS the column's role, and which
'     changes are legal is the template read's content: BR-60, SA 2026-10-16
'   - A NAME IS NOT A ROLE. Naming a lane cannot add a second Backlog, so the guard that asks
'     whether it would belongs to the role change and nowhere else; a new lane enters InProgress,
'     the role most added lanes carry, and is given another meaning by the role act: BR-58, BR-59,
'     `arch section 10`, SA 2026-10-18 ("naming a column does not change the column type, so the
'     'Would this add a second Backlog?' belongs to the 'Set the column's role' system response
'     path")
'   - A ROLE CHANGE WRITES THE CARDS IN THAT LANE. Their state follows the lane's new role - done
'     where it becomes Done, waiting or in motion where it leaves Done for Todo or InProgress - and
'     that is a STEP, not a note: a drawn note may not be the only place flow-relevant information
'     lives, because a note can be deleted and a box cannot: SA 2026-10-18 ("This is a step. The
'     comments must not contain flow-relevant information ... losing flow-relevant information
'     would be terrible"). The new role is never Backlog - the Backlog's role cannot change and no
'     change may add a second (BR-59, BR-60) - so the three states a card can be set to are the
'     three the lane can take. No history is rewritten by any of it (BR-124). What a role change
'     into Done CAN do is leave an activity with nothing open, which raises the same
'     completion offer a last move into Done raises on the board (BP11), answered activity by
'     activity because the change reaches every board the template governs. It fires exactly where
'     nothing is left open, so there is nothing for BR-127 to disclose and the closing carries no
'     answer about open cards, unlike the board's: BR-60, BR-109, BR-127, BR-108,
'     `arch section 10` ("InProgress -> Done: tasks suddenly count as done"), SA 2026-10-18
'   - the template read keeps reading and calculating apart and ends on its report, like every
'     other view read: BB01, SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
' Scope: this process shapes the lanes. What travels through them is BP11's, and nothing here
' touches a task's priority or its order.
'
' Call-site collapsing: inserting before and inserting after a column are two variations of one
' request. Configuring a project's template and configuring Chores's own template are likewise
' one request: the gesture is the same and only the owner differs.

pool "User" {
  start "The lanes no longer fit the work"
  :Work a column;
  rule BR-118

  if "What needs doing?" then "add a lane, or rename one"
    :Name the column;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the column;
    send "Edit a column" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as recorded
    note "A name is the user's word for the lane; renaming never changes what an existing lane means. Where a new lane lands in the order is the ordering's business (BP12.04)."
    end "Column recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "reorder them"
    :Order a column;
    send "Reorder columns" to reorderIn
    receive "The ordering outcome" as reordered
    end "Columns ordered"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "change what a lane means"
    :Set the column's role;
    send "Change a column's role" to roleIn
    receive "The role-change outcome" as roleSet
    note "Reaches every board the template governs (BR-108), which is why more than one activity can be left with nothing open."
    if "Did the change leave an activity with no card still open?" rule BR-109 then "yes"
      if "Mark the activity Done?" rule BR-109 then "yes"
        :Mark the activity Done;
        multiInstance
        rule BR-127
        send "Set the activity Done" to activityIn
        receive "The state-change outcome" as activitySet
        note "Answered activity by activity where the change completed several boards. A board the change completed has nothing open on it, so there is nothing to disclose and nothing to answer with the closing; declining leaves the activity InProgress, to be closed by hand on the Course page."
        end "Activities closed"
      else "no"
        end "Activity left in progress"
      endif
    else "no"
      end "Column role set"
    endif

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "clear out a lane"
    :Archive everything in the column on this board;
    send "Archive a column's tasks" to archiveIn
    receive "The archiving outcome" as archived
    note "This is the archiving act that takes a whole column's worth at once, on the board in front of the user. The column itself stays."
    end "Lane cleared"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "remove a lane"
    :Delete a column;
    send "See what deleting a column takes" to impactIn
    receive "What the deletion will take" as impact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-18 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete a column" to deleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as deleted
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Column deleted"
  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Column submitted" as editIn
  call "BP12.02_RenameColumn" "Edit a column" {
    :Store the edit, and set a new lane to InProgress;
    rule BR-58
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to recorded
  note "A name is not a role (BR-58), so nothing here can touch the one Backlog or the last Done (BR-59). InProgress is the role most added lanes carry (`arch section 10`); saying a new lane means something else is the role act's own business. A new lane appears on every board the template governs (BR-108), and the check-out and the advisor read a lane's role, never its name."
  end "Column answered"

  messageStart "Column reordering requested" as reorderIn
  call "BP12.04_ReorderColumns" "Reorder columns" {
    :Apply the new order;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The ordering outcome" to reordered
  end "Column reordering answered"

  messageStart "Role submitted" as roleIn
  call "BP12.05_ChangeColumnRole" "Change a column's role" {
    if "May this column take the role the request names?" rule BR-60 then "yes"
      :Record the column's new role;
      rule BR-58
      :Set every card in that lane to the state the new role gives it;
      rule BR-60
      rule BR-58
    else "no"
      :Refuse the change and say why;
      rule BR-59
    endif
    :Report the outcome, and which activities the change left with no card still open;
    rule BR-109
  }
  send "The role-change outcome" to roleSet
  note "Within BR-59 and BR-60's limits the consequences are the user's. No history is rewritten: what any span recorded as completed stands (BR-124)."
  end "Role answered"

  messageStart "Activity state submitted" as activityIn
  call "BP12.10_SetTheActivityDone" "Set the activity Done" {
    :Record the state the request names;
    rule BR-109
    rule BR-127
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The state-change outcome" to activitySet
  note "The Course page owns an activity's state (BP18); this is the completion offer answered from the column settings, as the board answers its own (BP11). A Done activity can be reopened there."
  end "Activity state answered"

  messageStart "Column archiving requested" as archiveIn
  call "BP12.06_ArchiveColumnTasks" "Archive a column's tasks" {
    :Archive every task in the column on the board the request names;
    rule BR-23
    rule BR-61
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The archiving outcome" to archived
  note "Archiving is a conscious gesture here as everywhere: no task archives itself. This act reaches the one board the user is on, unlike a change to the template itself."
  end "Column archiving answered"

  messageStart "Deletion impact requested" as impactIn
  call "BP12.07_ReadTheColumnDeletionImpact" "See what deleting a column takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take board by board, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-18
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-108
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the deletion will take" to impact
  note "A task cannot be left without a column, so the cascade is approve-or-abandon and detaching is not offered. Deleting a lane deletes it on every board the template governs, so the disclosure counts all of them. A column empty everywhere has nothing to disclose and deletes cleanly."
  end "Impact answered"

  messageStart "Column deletion requested" as deleteIn
  call "BP12.08_DeleteColumn" "Delete a column" {
    if "Is this the Backlog or the last Done?" rule BR-59 then "yes"
      :Refuse the deletion and say why;
    else "no"
      :Delete confirmed items;
      rule BR-18
      rule BR-108
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to deleted
  note "The Backlog column and the last Done column are refused with their reason, for the same reason their roles cannot change."
  end "Column deletion answered"
}

@endbpmn
